WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:07.749
"You'll love horseback riding, Grace," Daisy said.

2
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:13.457
Kaleem nodded. "It's so fun!"

3
00:00:13.458 --> 00:00:18.009
The kids were walking toward Our Little Farm.

4
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:23.041
Jan and Jon had invited them to meet some new animals and go riding.

5
00:00:23.042 --> 00:00:26.537
Beatrice sat quietly on Daisy's headband.

6
00:00:26.538 --> 00:00:31.999
Grace bit her lip. "Riding seems scary."

7
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.644
"Maybe at first," Kaleem said.

8
00:00:34.645 --> 00:00:39.957
"But you'll get used to it. Daisy and I ride on the beach during our vacation."

9
00:00:39.958 --> 00:00:47.916
Daisy nodded. "I can't wait. Summer will be here soon!"

10
00:00:47.917 --> 00:00:53.653
Jan and Jon waved as the kids approached.

11
00:00:53.654 --> 00:01:01.749
"Come meet our new pig, Hubert," Jon said, leading everyone to a new pigpen.

12
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:06.978
"Uh-oh! Hubert's trying to get out!" Kaleem said.

13
00:01:06.979 --> 00:01:11.666
Jon rushed to close the gate.

14
00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:14.719
"He escaped twice yesterday.

15
00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:19.532
I guess I'd better fix the gate today." He sighed.

16
00:01:19.533 --> 00:01:22.359
"I was hoping to plant vegetables instead.

17
00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.903
There's so much to do on this farm!"

18
00:01:24.904 --> 00:01:28.395
"I can help you while the girls ride," Kaleem said.

19
00:01:28.396 --> 00:01:32.272
"Really?" Jon said. "That would be great!"

20
00:01:32.273 --> 00:01:34.226
"Sure," Kaleem said.

21
00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:37.880
"I've never fixed a pigpen or planted vegetables before.

22
00:01:37.881 --> 00:01:39.582
It'll be interesting."

23
00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:44.079
Beatrice suddenly buzzed in Daisy's ear.

24
00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:49.890
"A vegetable garden does sound interesting. I think I'll stay with Kaleem."

25
00:01:49.891 --> 00:01:53.582
"Okay," Daisy said. "See you later."

26
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:58.520
Grace suddenly glanced over. "Who are you talking to?"

27
00:01:58.521 --> 00:02:10.457
Daisy laughed. "Myself! I do that sometimes."

28
00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:17.166
Jan led the girls to another stable, where four horses were tied.

29
00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:25.666
"We have a new horse named Sunny and a new pony named Blossom," Jan said.

30
00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:29.082
"Sunny is so pretty!" Daisy said.

31
00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:34.554
Jan nodded. "He's called a palomino because of his golden coat."

32
00:02:34.555 --> 00:02:38.413
Sunny whickered. "Hi there. I'm new!"

33
00:02:38.414 --> 00:02:41.209
Daisy went over to pat Sunny.

34
00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:47.582
"I'm Daisy," she whispered. "I can understand you when you talk."

35
00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:52.561
Sunny flicked his tail. "Whoa! That's great!"

36
00:02:52.562 --> 00:02:57.499
Daisy turned to Jan. "Can I ride Sunny today?"

37
00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:02.871
"Sorry, no," Jan said. "He's young and green."

38
00:03:02.872 --> 00:03:09.738
"Green?" Grace looked confused. "I thought you said he was a palomino!"

39
00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:17.121
Jan laughed. "We call a horse 'green' when he's not fully trained yet.

40
00:03:17.122 --> 00:03:21.736
A horse dealer talked us into trying Sunny out for a while.

41
00:03:21.737 --> 00:03:27.176
But Jon thinks it will take too long to train him." She looked sad.

42
00:03:27.177 --> 00:03:32.913
"Jon wants to send Sunny back when the dealer returns today to check on him."

43
00:03:32.914 --> 00:03:38.267
Sunny whinnied gently. "I don't want to go back. I like it here."

44
00:03:38.268 --> 00:03:41.068
"I'll try to help you," Daisy whispered.

45
00:03:41.069 --> 00:03:46.041
"I just need to figure out how to change Jon's mind."

46
00:03:46.042 --> 00:03:49.025
"How about this, girls?" Jan said.

47
00:03:49.026 --> 00:03:53.249
"I'll give you a riding lesson before we go on a trail ride."

48
00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:59.541
"I've never ridden before," Grace said. "Can I ride the slowest horse?"

49
00:03:59.542 --> 00:04:03.314
"Sure. You can ride Blossom," Jan said.

50
00:04:03.315 --> 00:04:06.124
"She's very gentle with beginners.

51
00:04:06.125 --> 00:04:09.938
Sunny is better for more experienced riders."

52
00:04:09.939 --> 00:04:12.806
"I've ridden a lot," Daisy blurted out.

53
00:04:12.807 --> 00:04:17.749
"I've been on lots of different horses at the beach. All sizes too!"

54
00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:23.791
"Really?" Jan said in surprise. "I didn't know that, Daisy."

55
00:04:23.792 --> 00:04:25.692
Daisy looked down.

56
00:04:25.693 --> 00:04:29.892
She'd actually gone on only a few short beach rides.

57
00:04:29.893 --> 00:04:38.367
"Uh-oh," she thought. "I just told Jan a big, fat lie!"
